      {
        "id": 245259,
        "name": "",
        "username": "The_Justifier",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-06-02T11:38:56.035Z",
        "cooked": "<p>They finally read another of my letters, as I am the mind behind the mask of L. M. Mentalist.  The grab-bag of characters I named at the end of my letter was hastily and poorly chosen; Skateblade should actually have been Pool Shark, as that’s who I was thinking about.  Karnal is indeed one of the Spite clones, as Vertex is one of the axes I’m still grinding a bit; I want those characters to come back into canon somehow.  And I count Inductor as a new character because she didn’t just change name, but also gained new powers.</p>\n<p>PS, they missed or opted to drop one line from my letter, right after I asked about lingering mystery people from EE: “(No doubt if that last answer is yes, the fan demand to include these ultra-successful ninjas in one of DE’s later expansions will begin posthaste.)”.  Whether such persons exist remains uncertain; I can’t think of one, but I also don’t know any Terrorform hints in EE, so clearly I don’t <em>quite</em> know everything.  (But that will change once I gain the power to conspire with Wager Master and combine my universe with the Sentinel Comics multiverse, allowing the premier super team of my world to fight the Freedom Five and Unity over possession of twelve cosmically powerful artifacts before me and WM can get ahold of them for our reality-warping schemes.)</p>",
