        "created_at": "2026-01-08T15:16:40.289Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Craftmason would be a good word for people who make creative things, including games as well as puzzles and certain complex types of toys, all collectively known as “crafts”.</p>\n<p>I expected not to care about this episode, having never touched a Definitive Edition card, but the new music adds so much to the early part of the episode.  I’m definitely enjoying it more than I should.</p>\n<p>Oh hey, a fourth letter of mine.  L.M. Mentalist is probably my best work, other maybe than America’s Crappiest Legacy, and he’s both harder to justify using and a lot less fun.  Ted Doggett was my vanilla letter writer, with no gimmick.</p>\n<p>To clarify LMM’s question, I’m interested in knowing which early design concepts they’ve steered away from, from the original IHOP meeting to Sentinel Tactics to OblivAeon to The RPG to Definitive Edition.  I doubt that the original Infernal Relics design meeting had a ghost of a notion of Akash’Mecha in it, but we can be pretty sure that an early design had a character that was basically “Ra but sonic”, who became the Shrieker, who then became Glamor.  We definitely know the original Absolute Zero had mechanical design aspects that didn’t survive to Ryan Frost, and I wish they’d been fully spelled out.  I also wonder how far they got in starting to design Orthrus, and how much of that work eventually showed up for Plague Rat or Apex or Bugbear.  And when did they decide on teams?  Were they originally planning the Prime Wardens to include Ra and Visionary?  How about the original plan to have all five hero decks from the Vengeance box, including the Sentinels when they existed in the 90s, be the ones who canonically thwarted the Vengeance Five’s carefully calculated plan to kill the FV?  I really want to be able to fully document these alternate histories and make them all work, instead of only the version they currently accept as truth.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"29290\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>think it’s Swedish, which means the ‘sk’ is said more like an ‘sh’ and the ‘y’ is more like an ‘oo’.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Oh, so Shoewhale then.  That actually makes even less sense!</p>",
